<title>HONG KONG: Chinese Estates 1996 net jumps 145.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Chinese Estates 1996 net jumps 145.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   68.0	  vs  32.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    19.0	  vs  18.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  628.63 gain vs  23.23 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    1,256.47    vs  512.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		     3,256.55    vs  1,175.09</p>
<p>    Company name		 Chinese Estates Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 11-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 14</p>
<p>NOTE - Chinese Estates is a property investment firm.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$635.05 million on disposal of invetment and other properties, gain of HK$8.52 million on disposal of long-term investment and loss of HK$14.94 million on reorganisation expenses written off.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 30 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 11 cents) vs 29 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
